  "engineering_notes": [
    "Prototype component-level design; neither netlist checks nor manufacturer module approvals establish safety/EMC approval of the complete assembled controller.",
    "No Y capacitor, earth connection, or neutral connection to isolated GND. Keep hazardous-voltage traces separated from all sensor, MCU and service conductors by the project isolation barrier.",
    "R1/RV1 are an engineering variant of the RECOM surge example, not a qualified 2 kV solution. Verify impulse energy, continuous overvoltage behavior, thermal disconnect and upstream fault interruption.",
    "RACM06E-05SK/277 full-load rating at 115-277 VAC is 6 W up to 50 C local ambient, 5 W at 65 C. Use measured internal enclosure temperature and actual load for derating.",
    "Capacitor values are nominal. Qualify exact purchased MLCC part numbers for DC bias, tolerance, temperature and buck stability; generic entries are not procurement-release MPNs.",
    "Custom axial fuse/resistor footprints assume formed lead spacing. Fit-check purchased parts before fabrication; TMOV footprint specifically requires inline L2B7 lead suffix.",
    "Hardware watchdog, reset supervisor and relay fail-safe logic are defined on another sheet. MCU_EN is shared open-drain reset; RUN_CMD, PERMIT_D and HEARTBEAT require external safe-state pull-downs there.",
    "8 MB module antenna cable connector and external antenna are mechanical BOM items, not additional RF PCB circuitry. Follow module approval antenna requirements.",
    "R2 intentionally loads the 6 W supply above its 10% minimum for specified regulation: at least 0.677 W at 4.75 V, up to 0.844 W at 5.25 V, including 1% tolerance. Total conservative 5 V allocation is now 5.7 W including OLED and J34 expansion; constrain measured PSU local ambient to <=50 C. R2 datasheet 2 W rating assumes 300 mm2 combined pad/trace copper, with linear derating above 70 C to zero at 155 C. Verify resistor/PCB temperatures and keep its heat away from precision probe/meter circuitry, RF module and capacitors."
  ]
